\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The FLAIR model-to-data loop. A Model Owner develops against public MIMIC-CLIF and submits a frozen model, code, or container. The Benchmark Committee reviews it for reproducibility, clinical face validity, and security, and stamps a task audit hash. The FLAIR Portal distributes byte-identical code to participating CLIF sites, where a Site Lead or Data Steward runs it locally against site CLIF tables. Patient-level cohorts, features, and predictions remain inside the institutional boundary; only aggregate, cell-suppressed JSON report bundles return. The leaderboard foregrounds per-site variation rather than a single pooled scalar. Source: authors.}}{8}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:workflow}{{1}{8}{The FLAIR model-to-data loop. A Model Owner develops against public MIMIC-CLIF and submits a frozen model, code, or container. The Benchmark Committee reviews it for reproducibility, clinical face validity, and security, and stamps a task audit hash. The FLAIR Portal distributes byte-identical code to participating CLIF sites, where a Site Lead or Data Steward runs it locally against site CLIF tables. Patient-level cohorts, features, and predictions remain inside the institutional boundary; only aggregate, cell-suppressed JSON report bundles return. The leaderboard foregrounds per-site variation rather than a single pooled scalar. Source: authors}{figure.1}{}}
